{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\nimpl<'d, D: Domain> ValidationContext<'d, D> {\n    /// Borrow the inspection context shared by this criterion's operations.\n    pub fn inspection(&self) -> &InspectionContext<'d, D>;\n}\n```\n\n`ValidationContext::inspection()` exposes the execution's `InspectionContext`.\nThe SDK's supplied agent uses that same context for graph-node reads,\noutgoing-edge queries, and delivery recording. The application supplies data\nthrough its domain; the SDK supplies and dispatches the tools.\n\nBorrowing the context does not record an input. The reads and edge selections\nperformed through it contribute the observations described below.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The structural obligations are met.\n\n**Accessor signature.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#1/fn[inspection]` is `pub fn inspection(&self) -> &InspectionContext<'d, D>`. It sits in an `impl<'d, D: Domain> ValidationContext<'d, D>` block, which matches the required signature.\n- It returns `&self.inspection`. That field is the `InspectionContext<'d, D>` that `ValidationContext::configured` creates, so the accessor exposes the execution's own context.\n- Borrowing does not record an input. The accessor only returns a reference and does not call `record_read` or `observe_edges`.\n\n**Supplied agent uses the same context.**\n- `Ask` holds `ctx: &ValidationContext`. `procedure.rs#impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, P>]#2/fn[execute]` calls `agent.run(request, &self.ctx.inspection)`. This passes the execution's own context, the one `inspection()` exposes, to the agent.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P, T>/Agent<D>]/fn[run]` receives that `&InspectionContext` and stores it in `GraphSession.inspection`. It does not create a separate context.\n- `GraphSession#impl[Conversation]/fn[dispatch]` then uses the shared context for the three operations the requirement names:\n  - `read_node` calls `inspection.prepare_read`.\n  - `outgoing_edges` calls `inspection.prepare_edges`.\n  - Page delivery goes through `deliver_page`, and `delivered` records the pending observations with `record_read` and `observe_edges` on the same context.\n- Unknown tool names go to `self.tools.dispatch`. Their dependencies join `pending`, so the SDK dispatches the tools, as the requirement says.\n\nI found no missing or conflicting structural element, and there are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments to account for.",
